From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: route MT7990 TX-free notifications from MAC

MT7990 does not have WA firmware and exposes dedicated MAC TX-free rings.
However, mt7996_mac_init() currently groups it with MT7992 and programs
UNI_RRO_SET_TXFREE_PATH to 1, selecting the WA path.  That disagrees with
the dedicated MAC ring configured for MT7990 and prevents the expected
TX-free notifications from reaching it.

MediaTek's MT7990 implementation defines path 0 as MAC and path 1 as WA,
and selects the MAC path for MT7990.  Select the WA path only for MT7992;
MT7996 and MT7990 continue through the MAC path.  This preserves the
existing behaviour for MT7996 and MT7992 while correcting MT7990.

The reference behavior comes from MediaTek's current MT7990 token and WED
implementation; this patch is the narrow adaptation for upstream mt76.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/671c2416d6219beb19abbb05709e418a6363be62/autobuild/unified/filogic/mac80211/25.12/files/package/kernel/mt76/patches/0054-mtk-mt76-add-debug-tools.patch
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/init.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/init.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/mt7996/init.c
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/init.c
@@ -655,7 +655,7 @@ void mt7996_mac_init(struct mt7996_dev *
 		mt7996_mcu_set_rro(dev, UNI_RRO_SET_BYPASS_MODE,
 				   is_mt7996(&dev->mt76) ? 1 : 2);
 		mt7996_mcu_set_rro(dev, UNI_RRO_SET_TXFREE_PATH,
-				   !is_mt7996(&dev->mt76));
+				   is_mt7992(&dev->mt76));
 	} else {
 		mt7996_mcu_set_rro(dev, UNI_RRO_SET_BYPASS_MODE, 3);
 		mt7996_mcu_set_rro(dev, UNI_RRO_SET_TXFREE_PATH, 1);
